    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is headlined by **Mickey Moniak** (74.56) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.65). **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% platoon advantage and favorable wind conditions, while **Tyler Soderstrom** draws a generous 10% park boost against Rocker, making them our primary targets for HR and RBI production. **Seiya Suzuki** (67.64) also presents a high-floor start, capitalizing on an advantageous matchup against the lefty Liberatore. We are navigating a difficult environment for **Gabriel Moreno** (43.69) and **Corbin Carroll** (52.07), both of whom are facing the elite arm of Sale. While **Corbin Carroll** remains in the lineup due to his irreplaceable speed profile\u2014a critical asset given our league's scarcity of SBs\u2014the 19% downgrade from Sale\u2019s xERA makes him a volatility risk despite his order-driven upside.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Isaac Paredes** (56.04) and **Travis Bazzana** (54.67). While **Isaac Paredes** holds a slightly higher score, the decision to prioritize **Travis Bazzana** in the 2B slot hinges on the positional flexibility required to optimize our core. **Austin Riley** (61.93) retains his spot despite batting 8th, as his 14% skill-matchup advantage and the potential for a \"slow delivery\" bonus\u2014which aids his SB upside\u2014keep him well above the marginal threshold. We are monitoring the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential rotation updates. We remain sidelined by injuries to **James Wood** and **Trevor Story**, while **Jose Caballero** and **Brice Turang** are currently benched as they rotate out of their respective starting lineups, forcing us to lean heavily on the current active configuration to maintain our Roto standing.",
